{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["He found him — like ״ומצא להם״. The Holy One, blessed be He, was found to them. The Holy One, blessed be He, was their provision." "He compassed him about — with His angels who guarded them. As written: ״חונה מלאך ה׳ סביב ליראיו ויחלצם״, and so the liturgical poet composed: ״לנו מלאכיך סביב יחנה״. And one who explains it as a surrounding of clouds is mistaken, for by the plain sense the cloud was nothing but a pillar of cloud going before them, as written: ״וה׳ הולך לפניהם יומם בעמוד ענן לנחותם הדרך״. And further, 'he guarded him' — a doubling of 'he compassed him about'." "As the apple of His eye — the Holy One, blessed be He, guarded Israel like the pupil that protects the eye. It is the flesh that covers the eye, which is called *pelpira*. And because it covers the eye and darkens it, it is called אישון, and similarly: ״שמרני כאישון בת עין״. ״כנוגע כבבת עינו״ — this is what is called *prunela*, through which one sees."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "Old French glosses: פלפיירא = pelpira (eyelid), פרונילא = prunela (pupil/lens)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:48.423827425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}